&lt;p&gt;Security researcher and AI practitioner. Creator of &lt;a href="https://imforster.github.io/llm-wiki/docs/entities/fabric/"&gt;fabric&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://imforster.github.io/llm-wiki/docs/entities/pai/"&gt;pai&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="relevant-work"&gt;Relevant Work&lt;a class="anchor" href="#relevant-work"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://imforster.github.io/llm-wiki/docs/entities/fabric/"&gt;fabric&lt;/a&gt; — Open-source framework with 251+ curated AI prompt patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://imforster.github.io/llm-wiki/docs/entities/pai/"&gt;pai&lt;/a&gt; — Personal AI Infrastructure built on &lt;a href="https://imforster.github.io/llm-wiki/docs/entities/claude-code/"&gt;claude-code&lt;/a&gt;. Persistent memory, skills, goals, continuous learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The two projects are complementary: Fabric = patterns (what to ask AI). PAI = infrastructure (how the AI operates).&lt;/p&gt;
